    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (69.34) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.38). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most reliable anchor against Castillo, leveraging an elite .421 xwOBA that keeps him as a must-start regardless of the matchup, while **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable position in the two-hole against Suarez. **Trea Turner** (65.75) also commands attention; while he faces a slightly tougher hurdle against a left-handed arm, his potential to catalyze the offense from the leadoff spot and his high-upside speed makes him a critical cog in our 5x5 Roto chase for stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision occurred at the Catcher/Utility threshold, where **Dillon Dingler** (33.13) fell well short of our 40-point efficiency floor. Despite a favorable lineup position, the combination of a sharp pitching opponent in McLean and a significant negative platoon adjustment effectively disqualified **Dillon Dingler** in favor of more efficient daily output. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the status of **Casey Schmitt**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; these spots are currently optimized based on pending lineup assumptions. We are particularly concerned about **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (41.99), who carries the highest risk today as he faces the elite arm of Sale. Should those lineups fluctuate, we will be forced to pivot, as our current strategy prioritizes plate appearances that yield efficient R/HR/RBI contributions while aggressively protecting our remaining game cap allocation.",
